Private copy (hygiene2), calling mod._refresh_regime_labels() exactly as the startup thread does:
- rows 4,189 -> 4,088; range 2010-01-26..2026-09-23 -> 2010-02-02..2026-06-18, so 101 recent labels were deleted;
- labels changed on 1,320 of 4,088 common dates;
- regime mix {R1 68.0%, R2 21.8%, R0 10.2%} -> {R1 56.5%, R2 40.9%, R0 2.6%};
- `git status` shows ` M data_store/signals/regime_labels.parquet`;
- `pytest test_c21_audit_fixes.py` then fails: test_adaptive_gate_reproduces_shipped_labels gives `assert 0.6771 > 0.99`.
The committed DB's max(spx_ohlcv.date) = 2026-06-18, so the staleness check `last_date >= today - 3d` is false on any clone.

findings.description:
The production bot hand-rolls its own option-chain fetch, while the dashboard's refresh thread uses DataPipeline and yf_downloader. Differences:
(a) expiries: first 8 (cloud) vs all (pipeline);
(b) liquidity: no spread filter and mid falls back to lastPrice (cloud) vs bid/ask spread < 20% of mid and mid from bid/ask only (pipeline);
(c) snapshot_date: closed SPX session (cloud) vs datetime.today() in local time (pipeline), so a run in IST after 05:30 stamps session+1 and get_options_surface(as_of=session) excludes it;
(d) VIX TS: pipeline calls download_vix_term_structure(start=...) with no end, which defaults to yesterday, so the just-closed session is dropped (the bug 236509e fixed only in cloud_refresh);
(e) VIX daily: Yahoo (cloud) vs CBOE CDN (pipeline);
(f) SPX window: 400 days vs 5 days, which leaves the gap from the committed DB untouched;
(g) DataPipeline.historical_backfill stops at config.HIST_END = 2025-12-31.
insert_options_snapshot is a plain INSERT despite the module docstring 'Write functions are idempotent'. cloud_refresh works around this with a DELETE; pipeline does not, so repeated dashboard refreshes duplicate chains.
